  "scope": "The isolated startup diagnostic flag records bounded timestamps and process memory/CPU at exact workspace, credential, persistent-cache, recovery, services, automation and window stages. Failure discovery adds a separately timed later process/phase probe without changing the original 30-second deadline. In isolated diagnostic mode an initialization failure logs phase/resources and exits with code 1 instead of waiting for an unattended native error dialog; ordinary production startup retains its native error UI. Disabled, ordered/immutable/bounded/default sampler and exact vault boundary tests pass. Two actual corrupt-file Electron processes exit in 268/246 ms with exact phases and no private input logged. All 653 component-source tests, type/build and six actual 84 MB backup checks including successful restart pass. The older focused backup writer has no normal-close field. The earlier hosted startup timeout cause is not established; fresh combined template/diagnostic source, complete 215-check body, distribution and hosted acceptance remain separate."
